# Line endings, pinned. Without this, Git's Windows default core.autocrlf=true
# checks every .ts and cep-plugin/bridge-cep.js out as CRLF, and the suites that
# compare generated text exactly (docs-drift, generated-script-syntax) fail on a
# Windows clone for a reason that has nothing to do with the code. Pinning LF is
# a prerequisite for Windows CI, not a style preference.
* text=auto eol=lf

# CRLF is the PowerShell convention and PowerShell reads either, so the scripts
# match what a Windows maintainer's editor will produce.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.zxp binary
*.mcpb binary
*.p12 binary
